"zeipagbu" can't be a lujvo. It will /always/ break into "zei pagbu",
because a lujvo must have a consonant cluster within the first 5 letters.
"zeipagbu" doesn't have a cluster until the 6th letter. In order to make a
lujvo of "zekri pagbu", you have to use the /other/ rafsi of xekri, "zer".

On Sun, Apr 15, 2012 at 5:28 AM, gleki <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com> wrote:

> Look at this example from jbovlaste.
>
> simfoni zei pagbu - p1 is a movement of symphony number k3 in key k4
> composed by k5.
>
> I wonder whether in spoken pauseless speech
> it can be mixed with
> simfoni zeipagbu  - which can be intrepreted as "symphonical crime-part".
>
> Do you have any explanation or solution?
